experiment: axisgrid
  instrument        axisgrid   trial seed 0000000001358e18   12 creatures
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  the question      how many INDEPENDENT steerable axes does the larynx
                    have? aimaxes measured 2 of the 9 groups senses.cpp
                    maps. Levels MULTIPLY across independent axes, so the
                    axis COUNT is the lever, not any axis's range.
  why it matters    retention is nearly FREE across an orthogonal axis
                    (axisfree 0.948 vs -0.167 on-axis, +5.7 SE), so the
                    number of lessons the creature can HOLD is the number
                    of axes it has. This is the accumulation lever.
  CLAUSE ORDER      1 liveness, 2 cross-talk, 3 resolution, 4 the product.
                    LIVENESS IS FIRST BECAUSE CROSS-TALK IS A RATIO: a DEAD
                    axis has zero cross-talk trivially and would be reported
                    as ideally independent. Pre-registered, not patched in.

  ZERO-RUNG IDENTITY  no bias is applied at k=0, so all nine groups run
  the SAME creature there. Largest disagreement across the nine: 0.000e+00  -> EXACT, as it must be

