    amp   reach     0.001 / scatter    0.091  ->   0.00 levels   (oracle swing/scatter   0.0)   (not in the product: not a vowel-identity axis)
    voi   reach     0.000 / scatter    0.095  ->   0.00 levels   (oracle swing/scatter   0.0)   (not in the product: not a vowel-identity axis)
    -> swing/scatter spans 6.2 to 6.5 across the live axes, i.e. NEARLY CONSTANT: the level count is the group ARCHITECTURE, not the parameter
    CAVEAT ON THE RULER, stated: `scatter` is WITHIN-RUN jitter, which is
    aimaxes's convention and so comparable to its 2.6 -- but a held vowel is
    scored over many ticks, so it OVERSTATES the noise a scorer sees, while
    the quantity that actually bounds naming is BETWEEN-TRIAL spread, which
    this run does not measure. Conservative, and the wrong ruler either way.

